WEBVTT

00:00:04.830 --> 00:00:10.420
The following program is intended for mature audiences
and contains Adult Content, Graphic Language,

00:00:10.510 --> 00:00:14.760
Graphic Violence, Brief Nudity
and Strong Sexual Content including rape.

00:00:19.810 --> 00:00:21.600
Take a look.

00:00:21.680 --> 00:00:25.060
The transplanted wrist
has manifested immortality as well.

00:00:27.400 --> 00:00:30.530
If we can replicate this with the rest of the limbs...

00:00:30.610 --> 00:00:32.570
Hold on a second.

00:00:32.650 --> 00:00:36.450
Don't tell me you intend to chop them all off?

00:00:36.530 --> 00:00:41.080
You don't actually enjoy
slicing up people's bodies, do you?

00:00:42.080 --> 00:00:43.540
Nonsense.

00:00:43.620 --> 00:00:46.290
It's true you only exist for the purpose of research,

00:00:46.380 --> 00:00:49.130
but if there were anything
that could truly put you in danger,

00:00:49.210 --> 00:00:52.760
I would most certainly foresee it
and eliminate that risk.

00:00:53.760 --> 00:00:59.100
There is no one in this country who cares more
about your well-being than I do right now.

00:01:07.770 --> 00:01:10.690
That was some clever yet deceptive talk.

00:01:10.780 --> 00:01:12.360
I was being sincere.

00:01:23.200 --> 00:01:25.500
Blade of the Immortal

00:01:25.580 --> 00:01:27.960
One, two, three

00:01:29.340 --> 00:01:33.210
Undead tree

00:01:33.300 --> 00:01:34.720
What truth

00:01:35.880 --> 00:01:38.550
I'll come true

00:01:40.810 --> 00:01:46.060
Wow, wow, wow, wow

00:01:46.140 --> 00:01:49.770
And I see that bright light

00:01:51.320 --> 00:01:56.490
This is all I have

00:01:56.570 --> 00:02:00.740
What did you say? I know

00:02:00.830 --> 00:02:05.080
Why do you say?

00:02:06.290 --> 00:02:10.460
Hone the blade
Lie around

00:02:10.540 --> 00:02:13.920
Survive of vision

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:17.420
Death and pleasure are my future

00:02:17.510 --> 00:02:21.720
I got lost
I was lost

00:02:21.800 --> 00:02:25.350
Survive of vision

00:02:25.430 --> 00:02:28.810
Unfinished heaven

00:02:28.890 --> 00:02:32.610
Now fight to claim your wounds

00:02:32.690 --> 00:02:36.780
Don't know why
Don't know why

00:02:36.860 --> 00:02:41.070
Survive of vision

00:02:56.960 --> 00:03:01.680
Are you Yoshihiro Asaemon Yamada, sir?

00:03:01.760 --> 00:03:03.140
Indeed.

00:03:03.220 --> 00:03:05.810
We've eagerly awaited your arrival.

00:03:05.890 --> 00:03:08.480
I'm the one who's summoned you.

00:03:08.560 --> 00:03:10.850
My name is Burando Ayame.

00:03:10.940 --> 00:03:13.560
So, Mr. Ayame,

00:03:13.650 --> 00:03:15.820
where is the head I'll be severing today?

00:03:18.070 --> 00:03:20.070
About that...

00:03:20.150 --> 00:03:23.820
What's this? I'm to cut not heads, but limbs?

00:03:23.910 --> 00:03:26.540
Yes, that would be correct.

00:03:26.620 --> 00:03:28.910
If heads are out of the question,

00:03:29.000 --> 00:03:31.250
I'll assume that means no intestines either.

00:03:33.630 --> 00:03:37.340
You would deprive me of the screams
that follow the stroke of a blade?

00:03:37.420 --> 00:03:39.630
A most unsavory state of affairs.

00:03:39.720 --> 00:03:44.180
However, if it's a request from
none other than Lord Kagimura Habaki,

00:03:44.260 --> 00:03:50.060
I cannot refuse simply because my expectations
were betrayed. Is that accurate, sir?

00:03:53.350 --> 00:03:54.360
What?

00:04:01.570 --> 00:04:04.370
Day six. Both transplants were successful.

00:04:09.330 --> 00:04:11.410
There were two surgeries today.

00:04:11.500 --> 00:04:13.830
The return of both subjects' right arms,

00:04:13.920 --> 00:04:16.880
and then the stitching of their left arms.

00:04:25.590 --> 00:04:27.680
After a single flash of the sword,

00:04:27.760 --> 00:04:31.060
the muscle, radius and ulna, and nerves

00:04:31.140 --> 00:04:34.980
were left clearly exposed
at the end of the immortal's truncated left arm.

00:04:42.070 --> 00:04:45.410
As of now, today's surgery was a success.

00:04:45.490 --> 00:04:48.740
The remaining question
is of this immortality's duration.

00:04:48.830 --> 00:04:51.910
I will await Dewanosuke's recovery.

00:04:52.000 --> 00:04:56.460
Dewanosuke is drained of so much energy
after each surgery,

00:04:56.540 --> 00:04:57.790
while this man...

00:05:05.680 --> 00:05:06.800
It's a success.

00:05:08.550 --> 00:05:09.760
Thank goodness.

00:05:09.850 --> 00:05:13.430
I was unsure we would make it past this point.

00:05:15.730 --> 00:05:17.650
Doctor,

00:05:17.730 --> 00:05:21.440
you're a really incredible person.

00:05:25.110 --> 00:05:29.120
Do you think I'll acquire this undying body?

00:05:29.200 --> 00:05:31.160
What are you saying? Of course you will.

00:05:31.240 --> 00:05:34.120
All I need is for you to believe in me.

00:05:39.710 --> 00:05:41.800
By the way, Burando,

00:05:41.880 --> 00:05:44.550
today is the appointed eighth day.

00:05:47.130 --> 00:05:52.890
If you were to be removed at this stage,
your replacement would only find matters bewildering.

00:05:54.930 --> 00:05:58.190
Very well. I will permit you to resume your duties.

00:06:01.770 --> 00:06:03.230
My gratitude.

00:06:04.650 --> 00:06:06.280
If they become one, there will be two.

00:06:07.450 --> 00:06:09.530
If they become two, there can be three.

00:06:14.040 --> 00:06:17.000
Even with his fever this high?

00:06:17.080 --> 00:06:19.710
There was one thing I worried about in secret,

00:06:19.790 --> 00:06:24.300
that I was pushing them too hard to connect,
especially with one of their bodies being immortal.

00:06:24.380 --> 00:06:27.470
Okei, go wake Toraemon
and grab some smelling salts.

00:06:27.550 --> 00:06:29.760
Also some cane sugar in hot water.

00:06:29.840 --> 00:06:31.220
Hurry.

00:06:33.930 --> 00:06:36.680
Omitsu. Omitsu.

00:06:38.390 --> 00:06:40.850
It's his wife's name.

00:06:40.940 --> 00:06:43.440
His wife is his world.

00:06:43.520 --> 00:06:47.150
It's okay. You'll be better soon.

00:06:47.240 --> 00:06:51.070
I won't die. I won't die.

00:06:51.160 --> 00:06:52.780
Of course not.

00:06:52.870 --> 00:06:54.490
I will not allow it.

00:07:13.430 --> 00:07:14.970
Omitsu.

00:07:16.350 --> 00:07:18.270
Omitsu.

00:07:20.100 --> 00:07:22.060
Omitsu.

00:07:30.450 --> 00:07:32.280
It's time for the final test.

00:07:48.460 --> 00:07:50.260
It's finally come this far.

00:07:51.430 --> 00:07:52.680
No.

00:07:52.760 --> 00:07:56.390
That alone does not prove his immortality.

00:07:59.560 --> 00:08:00.560
Lord Habaki.

00:08:01.980 --> 00:08:04.350
Are you prepared, Dewanosuke?

00:08:04.440 --> 00:08:07.070
Just-- Just wait a moment, please.

00:08:07.150 --> 00:08:10.650
Wait? I'm merely testing his immortality.

00:08:10.740 --> 00:08:14.620
If you're telling me not to, what exactly does that say?

00:08:16.740 --> 00:08:18.580
Doctor,

00:08:18.660 --> 00:08:21.620
I'll be okay.

00:08:21.710 --> 00:08:26.340
You've gained my trust through this process.

00:08:26.420 --> 00:08:29.670
You cut me and I healed, right?

00:08:29.760 --> 00:08:33.880
The one thing that would make me certain
is if you told me not to worry.

00:08:33.970 --> 00:08:35.890
Don't let him do it, Burando.

00:08:35.970 --> 00:08:39.140
Through what eyes does this look immortal to you?

00:08:40.430 --> 00:08:44.350
Burando, if I'm waiting now
due to your lack of confidence,

00:08:44.440 --> 00:08:46.980
I had best rethink things as well,

00:08:47.060 --> 00:08:49.940
including your current role.

00:09:05.330 --> 00:09:06.580
Lord Habaki...

00:09:08.130 --> 00:09:09.750
put him to the test.

00:09:50.210 --> 00:09:51.630
He's dead.

00:09:54.880 --> 00:10:00.350
Burando, I will have another prisoner
ready for you within a few days.

00:10:00.430 --> 00:10:04.520
I will regard today's failure a special case
and overlook it.

00:10:04.600 --> 00:10:06.730
Next time there must be results.

00:10:11.730 --> 00:10:13.480
You fools.

00:10:14.230 --> 00:10:17.450
ORGAN AND LIMB MODIFICATION
FIRST TESTING: FAILURE

00:10:25.000 --> 00:10:27.250
Is the research progressing?

00:10:27.330 --> 00:10:30.790
No. Burando is still shaken.

00:10:30.880 --> 00:10:32.040
I see.

00:10:32.130 --> 00:10:37.720
I don't know how he can do what he does
and somehow be this delicate.

00:10:37.800 --> 00:10:40.470
That's not it, Mr. Karukozawa.

00:10:40.550 --> 00:10:43.310
It's because he's a doctor.

00:10:43.390 --> 00:10:46.180
Once a doctor and patient become intertwined...

00:10:47.480 --> 00:10:51.520
But holding the position of researcher
at the same time is eating away at him.

00:10:51.610 --> 00:10:52.650
DEAD

00:10:54.900 --> 00:10:57.490
There was no progress following that.

00:10:57.570 --> 00:11:01.700
I paid extra close attention
when performing the surgeries,

00:11:01.780 --> 00:11:05.080
but that failed in its entirety.

00:11:06.120 --> 00:11:07.750
Why?

00:11:07.830 --> 00:11:10.080
Why do they all die?

00:11:10.920 --> 00:11:12.040
DEATH

00:11:12.130 --> 00:11:16.000
Please, everyone, don't die!

00:11:19.420 --> 00:11:21.010
Hey, Burando.

00:11:22.140 --> 00:11:27.270
Burando, you should have just failed earlier on
and been done with it.

00:11:28.310 --> 00:11:34.520
If you had, I wouldn't have come
to expect so much of you.

00:11:34.610 --> 00:11:37.730
The young, most promising doctor in the country,

00:11:37.820 --> 00:11:43.660
having studied Western medicine and come to question
the medical practices in this country.

00:11:45.410 --> 00:11:51.500
But when you remove the veneer,
all you see is a murderer who's killed six criminals.

00:11:52.710 --> 00:11:55.920
What did you go to the Netherlands to accomplish?

00:11:57.130 --> 00:11:59.840
Remember, Burando.

00:11:59.920 --> 00:12:06.390
I haven't forgotten the you
who had just returned from the West,

00:12:06.470 --> 00:12:09.720
re-inspired, your eyes piercing through
everyone you met.

00:12:10.730 --> 00:12:12.350
The eyes of an investigator,

00:12:12.440 --> 00:12:18.820
one who said, "If we run out of death-row inmates
in the courtyard, just bring me the petty criminals."

00:12:20.570 --> 00:12:22.530
Exactly.

00:12:22.610 --> 00:12:26.030
If a person's insides resemble an otter's...

00:12:27.030 --> 00:12:29.200
That must be the truth.

00:12:29.290 --> 00:12:31.120
They are criminals.

00:12:31.200 --> 00:12:34.500
Otters who are and yet are not human.

00:12:35.880 --> 00:12:37.380
You have ten days.

00:12:37.460 --> 00:12:42.550
You had best decide
whether you're going to live as a killer or not.

00:12:43.550 --> 00:12:49.470
From here on, you must give up
on worrying about saving them.

00:12:52.850 --> 00:12:56.100
Have you bid your mother farewell, Jiro?

00:13:01.360 --> 00:13:02.990
What are you doing, Jiro?

00:13:03.070 --> 00:13:09.030
Mr. Goto, I've come along with you all this way
because you said I could be a practicing servant.

00:13:09.120 --> 00:13:10.330
Well, how about it?

00:13:10.410 --> 00:13:14.920
Instead, I'm locked up in an estate
endlessly mixing herbs that won't be helpful to anyone.

00:13:15.000 --> 00:13:16.880
Even during last year's flu outbreak,

00:13:16.960 --> 00:13:20.630
where acquaintances and friends
were dying one after another,

00:13:20.710 --> 00:13:23.550
the three of us were just content to watch over it all.

00:13:25.550 --> 00:13:27.590
With Mr. Osaki,

00:13:27.680 --> 00:13:30.140
and now Mother.

00:13:30.220 --> 00:13:33.350
Brother, you must understand too,

00:13:33.430 --> 00:13:38.100
that the majority of what this country calls medicine
is just good-luck charms.

00:13:38.190 --> 00:13:42.230
If we lived in a different country,
both Mother and Mr. Osaki...

00:13:42.320 --> 00:13:44.740
Our people are idiots! Our doctors, incompetent!

00:13:44.820 --> 00:13:47.110
-Know some shame, will you--?
-Jiro!

00:13:47.200 --> 00:13:48.780
I am a doctor.

00:13:55.830 --> 00:13:57.500
I am a doctor.

00:14:00.170 --> 00:14:01.750
I am a doctor.

00:14:04.420 --> 00:14:06.630
I am a doctor.

00:14:09.300 --> 00:14:10.930
I am a doctor.

00:14:13.520 --> 00:14:15.310
I am a doctor.

00:14:17.810 --> 00:14:19.730
I am a doctor.

00:14:22.360 --> 00:14:24.150
I am a doctor.

00:14:26.650 --> 00:14:28.320
I am a doctor.

00:14:30.950 --> 00:14:32.870
I am a doctor.

00:14:35.410 --> 00:14:36.960
I am a doctor.

00:14:39.750 --> 00:14:41.460
I am a doctor.

00:14:44.050 --> 00:14:45.510
I am a doctor.

00:14:48.130 --> 00:14:49.760
I am a doctor.

00:14:58.310 --> 00:15:00.690
You gave him ink?

00:15:00.770 --> 00:15:04.730
No. He most likely used the soy sauce from his meal.

00:15:20.330 --> 00:15:21.710
DEATH

00:15:30.220 --> 00:15:33.550
The leader must really overdo things.

00:15:33.640 --> 00:15:34.640
Here you go.

00:15:34.720 --> 00:15:38.810
That's right, he went and set a fire in a dojo.

00:15:39.810 --> 00:15:42.350
Oh, to be young again.

00:15:44.730 --> 00:15:47.730
So when will things happen?

00:15:47.820 --> 00:15:51.200
I was told it would be during the winter.

00:15:51.280 --> 00:15:53.070
Winter, huh?

00:15:54.780 --> 00:15:59.120
Will they make it all the way until then?

00:16:03.330 --> 00:16:06.040
Many days have passed now.

00:16:06.130 --> 00:16:08.920
Well, considering how many died,

00:16:09.010 --> 00:16:11.340
the suffering he feels as a doctor must be--

00:16:13.180 --> 00:16:15.140
Mr. Burando?

00:16:15.220 --> 00:16:17.390
Hi, Toraemon.

00:16:19.060 --> 00:16:21.230
Were you worried about me?

00:16:21.310 --> 00:16:23.480
I'll be counting on you again.

00:16:23.560 --> 00:16:25.150
Long time no see.

00:16:25.230 --> 00:16:26.900
Is that the next one?

00:16:28.110 --> 00:16:29.230
Yes. His name is--

00:16:29.320 --> 00:16:33.150
No, I don't need his name. More importantly,
we must prepare for the surgery.

00:16:34.320 --> 00:16:36.530
-Right.
-I'll need you to go request

00:16:36.620 --> 00:16:39.740
that Lord Habaki bring in the next criminal.

00:16:39.830 --> 00:16:42.210
What? The next one?

00:16:42.290 --> 00:16:46.540
Yes, because just one or two is too few.

00:16:49.210 --> 00:16:51.630
Where did you go last night?

00:16:51.720 --> 00:16:54.130
Oh, I was out searching again.

00:16:54.220 --> 00:16:56.050
What about you two?

00:16:56.140 --> 00:16:58.100
Oh, us?

00:16:58.180 --> 00:16:59.850
Get your hands off of me!

00:16:59.930 --> 00:17:02.730
-Quit struggling!
-The sake was strong, my fists threw themselves!

00:17:02.810 --> 00:17:05.190
Hasn't there been a lot of that recently?

00:17:05.270 --> 00:17:06.440
Yeah.

00:17:06.520 --> 00:17:08.860
Hey. You there.

00:17:08.940 --> 00:17:12.320
Just a second. Where are you three from?

00:17:12.400 --> 00:17:15.200
-You stand out like a sore thumb to me.
-Hey, what's going on?

00:17:16.450 --> 00:17:18.700
-Who are they?
-Not faces I know.

00:17:18.780 --> 00:17:19.950
Should we take them in?

00:17:20.030 --> 00:17:23.200
No, we're just...

00:17:24.580 --> 00:17:26.080
-Wait!
-Doa!

00:17:26.170 --> 00:17:31.960
Isaku, looking at their eyes,
I can tell they'll do something to us.

00:17:32.050 --> 00:17:33.050
This kid!

00:17:33.130 --> 00:17:37.300
Get ready. If leader were here,
he'd say this is the tipping point.

00:17:37.390 --> 00:17:38.720
-Right.
-What?

00:17:47.480 --> 00:17:49.190
-Take them!
-Don't move!

00:17:49.270 --> 00:17:51.360
Mr. Isaku, stop Doa!

00:17:51.440 --> 00:17:53.440
Killing a Hacchobori earns the death penalty!

00:17:53.530 --> 00:17:57.780
Miss Rin, thank you for your concern,

00:17:57.860 --> 00:18:01.450
but it's too late now.

00:18:01.530 --> 00:18:03.790
-What do you mean?
-Miss Rin.

00:18:04.790 --> 00:18:05.790
Surround them!

00:18:09.040 --> 00:18:10.420
Isaku!

00:18:16.260 --> 00:18:17.800
Stop!

00:18:23.600 --> 00:18:27.640
The two of us have killed people.

00:18:27.730 --> 00:18:30.360
Five. No, more.

00:18:40.070 --> 00:18:41.320
Doa!

00:18:53.590 --> 00:18:54.750
Hold it right there!

00:18:54.840 --> 00:18:58.090
Everyone, surrender immediately!

00:18:58.170 --> 00:19:00.470
You three will be arrested.

00:19:00.550 --> 00:19:03.600
You're kidding. Now what do we do?

00:19:04.600 --> 00:19:06.890
It's their fault for messing with us.

00:19:08.060 --> 00:19:09.140
At the ready!

00:19:11.100 --> 00:19:13.360
Take care of Doa, please.

00:19:21.490 --> 00:19:23.870
What are you doing? Don't let them get away!

00:19:23.950 --> 00:19:26.830
-Circle behind him!
-Get him!

00:19:29.620 --> 00:19:30.830
Isaku.

00:19:30.920 --> 00:19:32.880
Isaku!

00:19:41.130 --> 00:19:43.850
Doa, we should go check in at home.

00:19:46.720 --> 00:19:48.100
Are you crying?

00:19:49.480 --> 00:19:50.520
Shut up.

00:19:52.150 --> 00:19:54.360
What's come over you?

00:19:54.440 --> 00:19:56.110
Isaku.

00:19:56.190 --> 00:19:57.230
Isaku.

00:19:58.780 --> 00:20:00.610
Doa, listen.

00:20:00.700 --> 00:20:03.280
Mr. Isaku has only been captured.

00:20:03.360 --> 00:20:05.030
I'm sure he's fine.

00:20:05.120 --> 00:20:09.540
Right? Let's go home
and think of a way to rescue him.

00:20:09.620 --> 00:20:12.500
You don't understand a thing.

00:20:13.580 --> 00:20:16.840
Isaku is a Christian.

00:20:21.760 --> 00:20:24.640
It's okay. I'm sure it'll be fine.

00:20:25.970 --> 00:20:28.260
What'll be fine?

00:20:29.270 --> 00:20:32.600
You're weak, and I can't do it alone.

00:20:32.690 --> 00:20:35.060
What are you acting all weak for?

00:20:35.150 --> 00:20:36.770
You're Itto-ryu, aren't you?

00:20:38.860 --> 00:20:39.860
Why...?

00:20:41.900 --> 00:20:44.780
I knew it. That nonsense you're on about.

00:20:44.860 --> 00:20:47.490
It's identical to that of a guy I know.

00:20:49.240 --> 00:20:51.410
Think hard, Doa.

00:20:51.500 --> 00:20:56.460
Your leader would not be sitting here whining,
would he?

00:21:14.480 --> 00:21:18.190
Day 60. Fifteen perished today.

00:21:18.270 --> 00:21:22.860
There were no procedural errors
while severing at the elbow or stitching back together.

00:21:22.940 --> 00:21:25.780
The need for more samples has arisen.

00:21:27.660 --> 00:21:32.000
Does it reek? That's no good.
You'd better get used to it quick.

00:21:32.080 --> 00:21:38.920
Or is it perhaps that they still appear
as human to your eyes?

00:21:39.000 --> 00:21:40.170
DAY 62

00:21:40.250 --> 00:21:42.760
Day 62.

00:21:42.840 --> 00:21:45.470
Behold, Toraemon.

00:21:46.720 --> 00:21:48.140
Isn't this sort of nice?

00:21:48.220 --> 00:21:49.970
If you can't distinguish their faces,

00:21:50.050 --> 00:21:54.020
you don't have to empathize
with their life-or-death situation.

00:21:54.680 --> 00:21:56.310
Day 65.

00:21:56.390 --> 00:21:59.440
I've learned that there are distinct types of blood.

00:21:59.520 --> 00:22:03.690
I hypothesize that these blood affinities
play a large role in the failures.

00:22:03.780 --> 00:22:07.030
I request that next time
I be sent plenty with good affinities.

00:22:07.110 --> 00:22:12.580
The mystery of immortality is slowly unraveling
before my eyes. I can feel it on my skin.

